  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency WASH assistance to Cholera response through provision of integrated WASH services to IDP&apos;s , refugees and Host communities in Gedaref</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThis project is in&#xa0; line with identified needs and the priorities set under the Cholera response plan in Sudan.&#xa0;CARE will provide comprehensive WASH cholera response in Gadaref state targeting Medinat Al Gedaref,&#xa0;El Butana and El Rahad localities targeting 131,032 persons (49,454 Women , 31,450 Girls , 28,077 Men and 22,051 Boys). While&#xa0;CARE will implement the project directly with the&#xa0;State Ministry of Health (SMOH), the project is complementary&#xa0;to the&#xa0;PIU health response to Cholera in El Gadaref State and the&#xa0;same localities have been considered in the design of the CARE WASH response. CARE will also&#xa0;coordinate&#xa0;with&#xa0;other actors to jointly contribute to reducing morbidity and mortality due to Cholera and reduce the outbreak transmission in both the high-risk and the affected areas. The interventions will contribute to the objectives of the Sudan Cholera Response Plan. CARE will provide awareness-raising activities in the community on Cholera prevention and control, through public awareness activities and distribution of IEC materials.&#xa0;CARE will enhance WASH services inside CTCs in close coordination with PUI and complement the health services in the CTC and communities through the provision of&#xa0;cleaning and IPC materials,&#xa0;support&#xa0;solid waste management, water treatment (water chlorination and testing of FRC) along with hygiene promotion activities to enhance communities knowledge on cholera prevention and mitigation measures. This project utilizes&#xa0;CARE&#x2019;s multi-sectoral Cholera outbreak response strategy, which was developed by CARE in September 2023 and is currently implemented in Gadaref State.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
